{"metadata":{"symbolKind":"enum","externalID":"s:7IvorMXL15MXLStaffDetailsV4KindO","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"enum"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Kind"}],"extendedModule":"IvorMXL","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Kind"}],"title":"MXLStaffDetails.Kind","role":"symbol","roleHeading":"Enumeration","modules":[{"name":"IvorMXL"}]},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The staff-type value can be ossia, editorial, cue, alternate, or regular. An ossia staff represents music"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"that can be played instead of what appears on the regular staff. An editorial staff also represents musical"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"alternatives, but is created by an editor rather than the composer. It can be used for suggested","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"interpretations or alternatives from other sources. A cue staff represents music from another part. An","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"alternate staff shares the same music as the prior staff, but displayed differently (e.g., treble and bass","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"clef, standard notation and tablature). It is not included in playback. An alternate staff provides more","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"information to an application reading a file than encoding the same music in separate parts, so its use is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"preferred in this situation if feasible. A regular staff is the standard default staff-type.","type":"text"}],"sections":[],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLStaffDetails"]]},"relationshipsSections":[{"kind":"relationships","type":"conformsTo","identifiers":["doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/s8CopyableP","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/SQ","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/s9EscapableP","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/SH","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/s8SendableP","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/s16Sendab